{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1560159-best-dark-arcanoi-for-wraiths","id":1560159,"title":"Best Dark arcanoi for wraiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-22T20:10:33-07:00","id":1560159,"title":"Best Dark arcanoi for wraiths","content":"Whatts the best Dark Arcanoi for a wraith I t think Hive mind is best chow arcanois name was changed to something starting with C is best so you can poison thikr hivemind wijth bac intel","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-25T04:36:34-07:00","id":1560205,"title":"","content":"I don't know, tapping into the Spectre Hive Mind with a dominant Psyche seems like the fastest way to end up as one. With a strong Eidolon maybe, but even then the Shadow would probably do its best to reach out for assistance.<br /> <br /> If I had my pick, I would probably choose Tempest-Weaving. It's probably the closest you can get to open-ended sorcery as a Wraith, and so weirdly anti-entropic it makes me wonder how it ended up as a Dark Arcanos and not alternative Argos Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-30T16:09:33-07:00","id":1560275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1560159-best-dark-arcanoi-for-wraiths?p=1560205#post1560205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had my pick, I would probably choose Tempest-Weaving. It's probably the closest you can get to open-ended sorcery as a Wraith, and so weirdly anti-entropic it makes me wonder how it ended up as a Dark Arcanos and not alternative Argos Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tempest-Weaving probably has some of the best practical effects for a Dark Arcanos, but I would never call it anti-entropic. To my mind, it is definitely a manipulation of the entropy of the Tempest. It is heavily tied to Nihils which are holes in the fabric of reality. And its practical effects in terms of pulling lost objects out of the Tempest (which in itself is basically a Maelstrom) reflects that it has no set reality with time and distance being meaningless there. It is not about imposing order over chaos, or navigating your way to the safe byways still there, but using that it is sheer entropy to your advantage in a zen-like way.<br /> <br /> Like any Dark Arcanoi, it should be forbidden for most wraiths. And any exceptional wraiths who somehow manage to learn it, I'd make the wraith pay a heavy price for knowledge and use of it. Even in the description of the Tempest, we're told that wraiths encounter the fragments of thoughts and memories from lost, agonized souls and confronted with scenes of nightmare (which are probably the dead that immediately became spectres).<br /> <br /> One could argue that the highest powers of Larceny would be useful since those are anti-Oblivion, but I would rule as an ST that since it affects Composure and Psyche, they actually aren't applicable to wraiths, only spectres and thus would be useless to a wraith possessing them, leaving only the lower powers which are more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T03:37:36-07:00","id":1560282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1560159-best-dark-arcanoi-for-wraiths?p=1560275#post1560275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not about imposing order over chaos, or navigating your way to the safe byways still there, but using that it is sheer entropy to your advantage in a zen-like way.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't picking floatsam from or even shaping the noise of the Tempest (Chaos Carving) robbing Oblivion of its prize? Sure, eventually everything will be back on its way anyways, but for the brief moment a Spectre (or Wraith) is reversing that flow. Chaos Carving is very explicitly giving new form (order) to chaos.<br /> I agree though that in order to use the Arcanos, the Spectre has to be very 'in-tune' with entropy, something that would be difficult for a Wraith to maintain without falling to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-31T23:54:08-07:00","id":1560300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1560159-best-dark-arcanoi-for-wraiths?p=1560282#post1560282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't picking floatsam from or even shaping the noise of the Tempest (Chaos Carving) robbing Oblivion of its prize?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think so. Such objects can be encountered randomly during a normal travel in the Tempest. Or be deposited as flotsam after a Maelstrom hits the Shadowlands. It is just stuff caught in the Tempest like any junk found at sea or caught up in a whirlwind. It's not like these are things already swallowed by Oblivion. So Oblivion isn't &quot;robbed.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't see Tempest Weaving so much as &quot;imposing order&quot; as &quot;playing with chaos&quot;. Order, after all, implies you can't find shit if everything is messed up and mixed together. The ability of spectres to do so using Tempest Weaving means an affinity with entropy, not order. Just like the Hive-Mind doesn't imply some kind of Weaver aligned system of Drones (which, to be honest, has always bothered me. Order does not mean everything is the same. It means things can be differentiated from each other. It's also a problem I have with Clive Barker's insistence that Leviathan of Cenodite fame represents &quot;order.&quot; Wraith, in this regard, gets it right.)<br /> <br /> If that doesn't convince you, then it doesn't convince you. I just don't think Tempest Weaving is anti-entropic. I think it is very entropic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-01T02:16:22-07:00","id":1560302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1560159-best-dark-arcanoi-for-wraiths?p=1560300#post1560300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that doesn't convince you, then it doesn't convince you. I just don't think Tempest Weaving is anti-entropic. I think it is very entropic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that I need convincing, I'm just having a difficult time wrapping my head around it. Right now, I'm comparing it to Necromancy in that it uses entropic resonance to conjure/create something. I may be too locked into Mage thinking when I should come at it from Wraith, but that's a me-problem. <br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> Tangential, but I recall reading something about Stygia sending out relic vessels trawling for floatsam and plasmics in the Sea of Shadows. I like this very much as a set-piece for bringing some Innsmouth flavor to the setting, but I can't find the source. If anyone knows, please let me know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-01T13:02:25-07:00","id":1560306,"title":"","content":"I suppose it depends on how we are using the term 'entropic,' but I think the more important questions are how well does it connect to Oblivion or the state of being a spectre, and how much does it conflict with the state of being a wraith? On that front I'd say it is the least spectral of the Dark Arcanoi. Certainly with how many Spectres spend most of their time in the Tempest or below, it makes sense they'd be the main practitioners, but that seems to arise more from where they are than what they are. It's also worth noting that the ability to pull relics out of the storm was incorporated into the Wisp Horror set in Orpheus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}